VIETA'S FORMULAS
Coefficients already encode how the roots are related.
You do not have to solve the polynomial to know those relations.

FUNDAMENTALS
A polynomial of degree n has n roots (counting multiplicity, over C).
The coefficients are (up to sign and the leading coefficient a)
the elementary symmetric polynomials in those roots.
Named after François Viète (16th century).

VARIABLES
a, b, c, d, e  leading and remaining coefficients  (a ≠ 0)
α, β, γ, δ     roots

QUADRATIC
ax² + bx + c = 0
roots α, β

α + β  =  -b/a
αβ     =   c/a

CUBIC
ax³ + bx² + cx + d = 0
roots α, β, γ

α + β + γ           =  -b/a
αβ + αγ + βγ        =   c/a
αβγ                 =  -d/a

QUARTIC
ax⁴ + bx³ + cx² + dx + e = 0
roots α, β, γ, δ

α + β + γ + δ                         =  -b/a
αβ + αγ + αδ + βγ + βδ + γδ           =   c/a
αβγ + αβδ + αγδ + βγδ                 =  -d/a
αβγδ                                  =   e/a

PATTERN
For P(x) = a x^n + a_{n-1} x^{n-1} + ... + a_0
the k-th elementary symmetric sum of the roots
equals (-1)^k * a_{n-k} / a
